{
	"info": {
		"name": "Field Service System API",
		"description": "Complete API collection for the Field Service System. Run Register/Login first to save the access and refresh tokens as collection variables, then run each folder in flow order: Services -> Service Requests (Customer creates, Manager approves/rejects) -> Assignments (Manager assigns technician) -> Service Visits (Schedule, Technician Arrives/Starts, Work Completed) -> Invoices (Manager issues) -> Payments (initiate via /payments/initiate or /payments/:invoiceId/pay, then bKash redirect/webhook) -> Feedbacks (Customer reviews the completed + paid work order) -> Admin (users, roles, dashboard stats, audit logs). Users can read/update their own profile at /users/me. The core resource is exposed at /resources (CRUD + search + soft delete + assign/status/cancel/my-assigned). Completing a visit auto-completes the work order. Resource IDs are captured automatically via test scripts. Applicants register as customers, apply via Technicians -> Apply as Technician, then an Admin/Manager approves or rejects.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
